# LEAN-v21 variance partitioning

Fixed 23-chunk test set, 500 training chunks, harness ridge (per-electrode alpha by bootstrapped CV). Variance explained per electrode = r·|r| with r the canonical per-chunk-averaged Pearson r; averaged over electrodes. 95% CIs from a paired bootstrap over test chunks.

**60 of 135 fits missing** — tables below are partial.

## Full model: LEAN-v21 vs LEAN-v20

- grid: mean r = 0.0902, R² = 1.888% of variance | v20 mean r = 0.0904; Δr = -0.0003 [-0.0006, -0.0000]
- all166: mean r = 0.0805, R² = 1.581% of variance | v20 mean r = 0.0808; Δr = -0.0003 [-0.0006, +0.0000]

